Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs` to hook directly into native callbacks:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => {
            // Android OnPause — app losing focus
        })
        .OnStop(activity => {
            // Android OnStop — app fully backgrounded
        }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => {
            // iOS — app entered background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need the native parameters, you can use `Window.Stopped` which maps to `OnStop` on Android and `DidEnterBackground` on iOS:

```csharp
// In App.cs
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
{
    var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);
    window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* runs on background for both platforms */ };
    return window;
}
```

**Key notes:**
- `OnPause` (Android) = loss of focus (notification shade, split-screen) — maps to `Deactivated`, not `Stopped`.
- `OnStop` (Android) and `DidEnterBackground` (iOS) both map to `Window.Stopped`.
- Keep handlers fast (<2s) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS.
